	<string name="information_text">
		Developed and maintained by the Banchory Greenpower team, the OMNI telemetry app works with the eChook data logging and 
		telemetry system created by echook.uk for electric cars participating in the Greenpower Education Trust challenge. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		The app connects to the eChook using bluetooth to collect sensor data including battery voltage, current, motor rpm,
		speed, throttle, brake, and temperatures. The app calculates distance traveled and battery usage from the sensor data
		and acquires the car position. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		The data can be shown on a number of different dashboards in different sizes and device orientations to provide an in car display. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		The app logs the data every 0.25s to a file which can be shared or
		downloaded for later analysis. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		The app can also upload the telemetry data to a website, such as the eChook live data
		or a user defined location, to allow the data to be viewed in near real time during testing or racing.
	</string>

	<string name="support_text">
		The OMNI telemetry app continues to be developed and maintained by the Banchory Greenpower team. Your comments and feedback are most welcome. 
		We will endeavour to do our best to respond quickly. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		You are encouraged to use the eChook support forum for general discussions about the app, to report a bug, to suggest better non-English translations, 
		or to request a possible enhancement. 
		You can also email us on the email address below.
	</string>

	<string name="share_settings_text">
		This screen allows teams to easily transfer key car specific settings from one phone to another using a QR code.The code can be displayed on one
		phone and then scanned by another phone to which the settings are to be transferred. Alternatively the code can be shared and printed off, 
		laminated and attached to a car making it easier to ensure that the app is always set up correctly by scanning the code. 
		&lt;br />&lt;br />
		The QR code below contains the current settings saved on this phone. 
	</string>
	<string name="share_settings_permission_rationale">"Without camera permission it will not be possible to scan QR codes"</string>
	<string name="share_settings_alert">"Update settings to the following:"</string>

	<string name="developer_heading_set_state">Launch and lap counting</string>
	<string name="developer_desc2_set_state">Simulate pressing the launch button to reset state to waiting for the throttle to be depressed as when waiting for the race to start. In this state the GPS position of the start is acquired for lap counting.</string>
	<string name="developer_desc3_set_state">Simulate depressing the throttle and set state to running and start the race timer. In this state the current GPS position and the position of the start is used to calculate the current active lap.</string>

	<string name="set">Set</string>

	<string name="battery_optimisation_title">Disable battery optimisation (allow background usage)</string>
	<string name="battery_optimisation_message">Battery optimisation is currently enabled for the app, but needs to be disabled to allow 
		the app to continue to run when the app is inactive or the display is off. For some phones the setting for disabling battery 
		optimisation may be shown as allow background usage. If battery optimisation is not disabled the app will most likely run for 
		some time then simply stop functioning.
	</string>
	<string name="battery_optimisation_disallow">Disable battery optimisation</string>

	<string name="permissions_text">
		For the OMNI telemetry app to function correctly explicit permission has to be given to use precise location data, 
		to use a bluetooth connection, and to post notifications. Permission must be provided for all of these. &lt;br />&lt;br /> 
		&lt;b>Precise location data&lt;/b> permission allows the position of the car on the track to be determined. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		&lt;b>Nearby devices&lt;/b> permission allows a bluetooth connection to be made by the phone to a nearby device, for example an eChook, 
		to collect real time car sensor data such as voltages, current, speed, and temperatures. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		&lt;b>Notifications&lt;/b> permission allows the app to post a notification showing that location data and car sensor data are 
		still being collected even when the app is not visible or the display is off. &lt;br />&lt;br />
		The location data and car sensor data are saved to file on the phone for later analysis. The location data and
		car sensor data can also be optionally uploaded for displaying on remote telemetry displays.
	</string>	
	<string name="permissions_location_alert_title">Location permission</string>
	<string name="permissions_location_alert_message">
		Please select \'Allow all the time\' on the next screen to allow access to this device\'s location all the time, 
		even when the app is not visible or when the screen is turned off. Do not remove access to location on the next
		screen otherwise the app will terminate immediately (this is normal Android app behaviour!).
	</string>
